@using Odyssey.Dtos.Finance

@*
    OdsTransactionTagPicker — THE control for picking the transaction tag a record plans for
    (Odyssey Design System · components/TransactionTagPicker).

    Built for the budget item, where the tag is not a label on the item but the item's IDENTITY: the
    row's name, its description and the thing its actuals are summed from all come from the tag
    (issue #75).

    It is NOT a new widget. It wraps OdsCombobox in an OdsFieldShell — the pairing every labelled
    picker in the kit already uses — and adds only what a required, identity-bearing tag field needs:

      • The selected tag's DESCRIPTION becomes the help line. With no description it falls back to the
        standard helper, so the slot never renders empty — which is also what keeps the error line's
        id stable: OdsFieldShell moves the error to {HtmlFor}-help-error only while help is present,
        and aria-describedby names BOTH ids from the first render (the wiring is firstRender-only, so
        an id introduced on a failed submit would never be applied).
      • Tags already planned for are OFFERED but not selectable, marked with the trailing word
        "in use" — never a colour or an icon alone.
      • An archived tag reads "· Archived" in its option label, so the marker survives into the
        collapsed input and the accessible name. An archived tag is offered only when it is already
        this record's tag.
      • Inline create, gated TWICE: pass OnCreateTag only where the caller holds
        transactions.tags.create, and omit it on a surface with no submit to stage a create against —
        an inline grid that saves on change must not put an unresolved tag id on the wire.
      • Duplicate names are refused BEFORE the create is staged. Tag names are unique
        case-insensitively, archived rows included, so the picker checks the typed name against the
        list it already holds and renders the conflict at the field, naming the archived case, which
        has no inline remedy.

    HideLabel keeps the real <label for> association while removing it visually — for a grid cell
    whose column header is display:none at narrow widths and so is no accessible name at all.
*@

@* HtmlFor is withheld in the two states that render NO control (WCAG 1.3.1): the shell would
   otherwise emit `<label for="@InputId">` pointing at an id nothing in the DOM carries, since the
   combobox is what owns that id. A label with no `for` is a plain caption; a label naming a missing
   control is a broken association. *@
<OdsFieldShell Label="@Label" HtmlFor="@(HasControl ? InputId : null)" Required="Required"
               Help="@HelpText" Error="@ShownError" Class="@ShellClass">
    @if (LoadFailed)
    {
        @* Explicitly NOT the "create a tag" empty state: telling someone to create a tag when the
           list merely failed to load points them at the wrong problem. *@
        <div class="odc-tagpick-unavailable">
            <span>Unable to load the tag list.</span>
            @if (OnRetry.HasDelegate)
            {
                <button type="button" class="odc-tagpick-link" @onclick="OnRetry">Retry</button>
            }
        </div>
    }
    else if (NoneSelectable)
    {
        <div class="odc-tagpick-empty">
            <span>No tags left to plan for.</span>
            <a class="odc-tagpick-link" href="@ManageHref">@ManageLabel</a>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @* No clear (x): the tag IS the record's identity, so there is no "none" to clear to.
           OdsCombobox defaults Clearable to TRUE while the design system's Combobox defaults it to
           FALSE, so this has to be passed explicitly — without it the affordance blanks a required
           field. OdsCurrencySelect does the same for the same reason. *@
        <OdsCombobox InputId="@InputId"
                     Value="@SelectedValue"
                     ValueChanged="OnValueChanged"
                     Options="@Options"
                     Placeholder="@Placeholder"
                     Disabled="Disabled"
                     Required="Required"
                     Clearable="false"
                     Error="@(ShownError is not null)"
                     EmptyText="@EmptyText"
                     AriaDescribedBy="@DescribedBy"
                     OnCreate="@CreateHandler" />
    }
</OdsFieldShell>
